    <paragraph>For the following exercises, describe the local and end behavior of the functions.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="25" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{x}{2x + 1}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Local behavior: $$x\to - 1 2 + ,f(x)\to -\infty ,x\to - 1 2 - ,f(x)\to \infty x\to - 1 2 + ,f(x)\to -\infty ,x\to - 1 2 - ,f(x)\to \infty$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>End behavior: $$x\to \pm \infty ,f(x)\to 1 2 x\to \pm \infty ,f(x)\to 1 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
