    <heading level="1">Real-World Applications</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, express a rational function that describes the situation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="80" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>In the refugee camp hospital, a large mixing tank currently contains 200 gallons of water, into which 10 pounds of sugar have been mixed. A tap will open, pouring 10 gallons of water per minute into the tank at the same time sugar is poured into the tank at a rate of 3 pounds per minute. Find the concentration (pounds per gallon) of sugar in the tank after $$t$$ minutes.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="81" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>In the refugee camp hospital, a large mixing tank currently contains 300 gallons of water, into which 8 pounds of sugar have been mixed. A tap will open, pouring 20 gallons of water per minute into the tank at the same time sugar is poured into the tank at a rate of 2 pounds per minute. Find the concentration (pounds per gallon) of sugar in the tank after $$t$$ minutes.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$C(t)= 8+2t 300+20t C(t)= 8+2t 300+20t$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the given rational function to answer the question.</paragraph>
